<title>POLAND: ZEW RESUMES TRADE MONDAY AFTER FLOOD.</title>
<headline>ZEW RESUMES TRADE MONDAY AFTER FLOOD.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish electrode maker ZEW SA, suspended from bourse trade since July 10 due to flooding, will resume trade on Monday August 11 without the daily 10-percent price-fluctuation limit, the bourse said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Last month ZEW said it had incurred losses exceeding 50 million zlotys due to the flooding which hit southern Poland but would receive full insurance compensation.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
